# Nidan

**Before making any change, read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root.** It is the
source of truth for this codebase and is kept up to date. What follows is the
short version, so it applies even when that file is not open.

This is a finished, tested application (40 passing end-to-end tests), not a
scaffold. Treat existing code as deliberate. Prefer small reviewable changes.

## Never break these

1. **Consent is enforced at the data layer.** Every clinical read goes through
   the gated accessors in `src/lib/db/store.ts` (`caseSheetsFor`, `vitalsFor`,
   `documentsFor`, …), which call `assertAccess()` and write an audit row. Never
   read `db.caseSheets` and friends directly from a page, action or route.
   The SQL twin is `has_care_access()` in `supabase/migrations/006_governance.sql`
   — change the rule in one place, change it in both.
2. **Clinical records are append-only.** Finalised case sheets are immutable;
   corrections create a linked amendment. Never add a delete path.
3. **Time is IST wall-clock stored as UTC.** Always use `src/lib/tz.ts`. Never
   use `new Date().getHours()`, `.getDay()` or `.toISOString().slice(0,10)` for
   anything clinic-related.
4. **The public emergency card (`/e/[token]`) exposes exactly six things** —
   blood group, allergies, current medications, chronic conditions, organ donor
   status, emergency contacts. Never widen that slice.
5. **AI output is always labelled with `<AiLabel />`**, never auto-enters the
   record, never diagnoses or prescribes, and always has an offline fallback.
6. **Secrets are never prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_`.**
7. **`src/lib/db/seed.ts` and `supabase/seed.sql` describe the same world with
   the same UUIDs.** Keep them in sync. Never delete the mock store — it is the
   demo-day fallback.

## Conventions

- Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict. Server Components by
  default; `"use client"` only when state, effects or handlers are needed.
  Mutations are Server Actions in `src/app/actions/`.
- Tailwind v4. Use the CSS custom properties from `src/app/globals.css`
  (`var(--color-brand)`, `var(--color-ink-2)`, …). **Never hardcode a hex value.**
- Light is the default and the app ignores `prefers-color-scheme`; dark is
  opt-in via `<ThemeToggle />`. Text on a filled colour uses
  `--color-on-brand` / `--color-on-critical` / `--color-on-good`, never
  `text-white`. Permanently-dark chrome uses `--color-chrome`.
- Semantic colour is reserved for clinical meaning. `--color-critical` means
  allergy, emergency, out-of-range, destructive — nothing else. Never encode
  status by colour alone; pair it with an icon or label.
- Charts use `--chart-1` … `--chart-6`, a palette validated for colourblind
  separation in both themes. Do not substitute other hues.
- Every new patient-facing string goes into **both** catalogues in
  `src/lib/i18n.ts` (en and hi). Doctor clinical vocabulary stays English.
- 44×44px touch targets, 16px minimum body text on the patient app, visible
  focus rings, skeleton loaders rather than spinners, empty states with an
  action, destructive actions confirm.
- Comments explain *why*. Match the existing voice: direct, specific, no filler.

## After every change

```bash
npm run typecheck   # clean
npm run build       # compiles
npm run smoke       # 40 assertions, all pass
```

Never weaken a test assertion to make it pass. Never run
`npm audit fix --force` — `next` and `postcss` are pinned deliberately.
